ialiser exactly\"\n    );\n\n    // Post-conditions of one `run`: +1 floor, +1.0 bathrooms, bedrooms unchanged.\n    assert_eq!(h.floors(), 3);\n    assert_eq!(h.bedrooms(), 5);\n    assert_eq!(h.bathrooms(), 3.5);\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_z2m3j5w2iwhf6n762buknavxhvqrzsjnqlnoqk2u3lru6nufxiuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Eg8VPLGmUhVDpqhg6Zp8We","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Opsu7S/translation/tests/first_call_driver.rs","content":"//! CONFIGS.md row 22 — `driver` as the first symbol ever resolved and called.\n//!\n//! Own test binary (= own process) so the global is pristine and `driver`\n//! runs before `run` is ever called directly. This pins down the wrapper's\n//! composition (`run(x); run(x);`) against the static initialiser.\n//!\n//! Exactly ONE `#[test]` on purpose — see `first_call_run.rs`.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\n#[test]\nfn row22_pristine_state_first_ever_call_to_driver() {\n    let mut h = lock();\n    assert_eq!(h.floors(), 2);\n    assert_eq!(h.bedrooms(), 5);\n    assert_eq!(h.bathrooms(), 2.5);\n\n    // Use a non-zero argument so the \"applied twice\" behaviour is visible.\n    let out = h.driver(10, \"row22 pristine driver\");\n    let s = String::from_utf8(out).unwrap();\n\n    assert_eq!(\n        s,\n        // first run(10)\n        \"The house has 2 floors, 5 bedrooms, and 2.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 3 floors, 5 bedrooms, and 2.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 3 floors, 5 bedrooms, and 3.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 3 floors, 15 bedrooms, and 3.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         // second run(10)\n         The house has 3 floors, 15 bedrooms, and 3.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 4 floors, 15 bedrooms, and 3.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 4 floors, 15 bedrooms, and 4.5 bathrooms\\n\\\n         The house has 4 floors, 25 bedrooms, and 4.5 bathrooms\\n\"\n            .replace(\"         // second run(10)\\n\", \"\"),\n        \"driver() on pristine state must match the C byte-for-byte\"\n    );\n\n    assert_eq!(h.floors(), 4);\n    assert_eq!(h.bedrooms(), 25);\n    assert_eq!(h.bathrooms(), 4.5);\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":64227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1056,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45e07446-42e1-4ca1-9deb-05b1c2a9cf48","uuid":"66d5fd3b-5420-49e0-a422-00204420365b","timestamp":"2026-08-28T14:10:56.757Z"}
